          "id": "expand",
          "name": "Fill semantic node inventory",
          "role": "implementer",
          "executor": {
            "kind": "provider",
            "provider_id": "pi-specialist"
          },
          "retry": {
            "max_attempts": 10
          },
          "outputs_schema": {},
          "prompt_template": "Read analysis/request.txt completely with read_workflow_resource_chunk, starting at byte 0 and following each next_byte until complete. Use its numbered source, complete resource inventory, Host callable/dependency facts and shared semantic contract. Return exactly {\"proposal\":...} using workflow-semantic-blueprint/v6; do not execute the source task. Preserve every required source method, direct tool/code interface, transport, argument, stdin/file contract, condition, quality check and repair/approval boundary. Distinguish active duties from examples, tests and archive material through source evidence. Check both directions: retain required behavior and require source or user support for added work. Choose useful responsibility boundaries with complete downstream handoffs; keep tightly interleaved production and local diagnostic repair together. Ordinary sequential work uses Main with fresh isolated context; choose workers for source-required delegation, concurrency or Provider choice and review for independent inspection. Use configured difficulty profiles without inventing models or Provider IDs. Reuse suitable supplied artifacts and conclusions. Assign source sections and Host observations by supplied IDs; the Host projects exact interfaces, schemas, paths, resources, dependencies and execution mechanics. Emit only newly authored semantic results and bind existing inputs/tool results directly into their consumers. Missing future-Run answers must block concretely. Every approval names its activity.output subject and protected activities. Declare runtime_dependencies explicitly, including [] when none is required, and preserve conditional/artifact-only triggers. Source-required downstream rejection uses a structured bounded loop with complete feedback, fresh read-only exit review and final acceptance outside; local transport retry cannot implement it. A fresh read-only Main worker can review independently unless the source requires another Provider. Preserve accepted items while repairing failures. Omit unused empty collections and placeholders; the Host materializes their unique empty interpretation without changing supplied meaning. Resolve same-turn compiler diagnostics before resubmitting. On correction, read the Host repair packet, return stable-key changes for the complete finding set and preserve unrelated keys."
        },
